WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:05.190
Hearing that Hikari’s Pochama
had been kidnapped,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.070
Satoshi, Go, and Koharu
arrived in Sinnoh.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.200
But in the midst of
their investigation,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.080
Lucario and Inteleon were
kidnapped by Team Rocket.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.210
When they followed Team Rocket
through a shining Gate, they found...

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.380
What is it?

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.090
When I looked this morning,
the garden was full of blooming flowers.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:32.720
...a mysterious world, which looked exactly like
their usual world, yet was slightly different.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.930
She really does look just like you!

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:39.640
The other Hikari from that world
had taken Pochama.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.690
And then, Satoshi came across...

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.820
Me?!

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.820
It’s me?

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.450
I’m Satoshi!
What’s your name?

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.790
I... I’m Satoshi,
from Masara Town...

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.000
No, that’s my name.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.960
But... I’m Satoshi, too...

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.250
You’re me, too...?
What’s going on?

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.840
I-It’s not like I know, either...

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.090
Well, I have to go...

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.590
Hey, wait!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.720
I’m sorry!

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.890
Oh, let me explain.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:21.600
Picture another world
that’s just like this one...

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.110
That’s where we came from.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.940
Another world...

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.820
Professor Nanakamado
was talking about that, too...

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.990
Oh, Pikachu!

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.750
So you like Pikachu, too.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.250
Yeah. But my...

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.300
What’s wrong?

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.470
Look.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.180
This is my Pikachu.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:34.570
A Pokémon...

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.570
...turned back into an egg?!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.990
Yeah...

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.950
Time might be
flowing backwards...

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.040
Oh, that’s right!

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.250
Pikachu forgot a move earlier.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.040
That’s not good!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.710
My Pikachu started off
forgetting his moves,

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.500
and then he turned into a Pichu,
and then an egg...

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.470
What am I gonna do?!

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.970
Would you... go to the Masago Town
Pokémon Center with me?

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.350
Professor Nanakamado
is looking into what’s happening.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.970
The Pokémon Center?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.140
Got it.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:05.980
Come on out!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:12.980
Too heavy...

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.200
Thanks, Kairyu!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.160
You too, Gänger.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.290
Hold on!

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.160
Just quiet down and stand aside.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.040
But...

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.790
It’s Professor Nanakamado.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.090
Our job is complete.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.510
Okay, let’s go.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.760
Professor Nanakamado!

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:38.470
Go!

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.470
...<i>Two</i> Satoshis?!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.050
...<i>Two</i> Satoshis?!

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.390
There’s two Hikaris, too!

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:45.180
Pochama!

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:51.980
Stop right there, you two.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.440
And now there’s two
Professor Nanakamados...

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.110
Who are you?!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.990
If you ask us “Who are you?”...

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.620
We will not give our names,
but we will show you.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.290
Team Rocket!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.420
Those guys are trying to take
all the Pokémon that were here.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.300
What?!

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.800
We’re not letting you!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.970
We’re gonna win back
our Pokémon!

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.640
Get rid of these nuisances!

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.100
Understood.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.570
You’re not getting away!

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.320
Evil Pulse!

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.160
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.460
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.090
Time is going backwards...

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.270
You should put them in your Monster Balls,
just to be safe.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.140
That seems to slow down
the rewind.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.190
Right.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.070
Return, Rabbifoot, Sarunori!

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.780
You can go in here.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:28.370
But, if this keeps up,
our Pokémon will end up reverting to eggs, too...

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.120
And that’s not all.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.870
It’s not just plants and Pokémon
being rewound.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.250
We humans are being rewound, too!

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.170
<i>What?!</i>

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.960
We have to do something!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.340
Ms. Shirona said that Palkia might be
making space distort.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.260
If time is also distorting,
then Dialga might be involved, too!

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:53.520
Professor! How can we meet
Palkia and Dialga?

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:59.440
If you go to the Spear Pillars
at the summit of Mt. Tengan...

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.900
Still, it would not be easy...

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:06.570
But if we could have Palkia and Dialga
fix these weird distortions,

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.780
I bet our Pokémon
would go back to normal, too!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.830
Yeah!
And I’ll be right there with you!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:13.540
Thanks!

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.040
Are you serious?!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.460
Yes!

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.590
Your earnest hearts may just be
the key to meeting them.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.590
Get going.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.010
Okay!

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:29.800
Kairyu, Gänger,
help us out again!

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.320
They were even
in their Monster Balls...

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.610
Time is rewinding even faster!

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.860
Let’s use my Flygon and Ptera.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.030
I’m coming, too!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:51.830
Me, too!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.120
There’s not enough room
for everyone...

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.710
Please, go on ahead of us.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.830
We will follow behind you.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.420
Got it!

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.840
Okay, see you later!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.670
Of course! Just maybe...

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.090
Calling! Calling!

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:17.020
Well, we went through that weird hole,
but those creeps are nowhere to be seen.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.270
Ooh, my skin’s feeling all smooth.
What a great feeling!

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.650
Meowmthing strange’s
meowing meow...

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.360
Huh? What?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.610
What’s wrong, Nyarth?

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:33.790
Hey! What’s with all the meowing?

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.330
Wha—?! What’s going on here?!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.760
So these are...
the Spear Pillars?

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.390
Dialga! Palkia!

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.730
Come out if you can hear me!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.860
It’s a Gate!

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.160
You’re right!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.700
Are they on the other side?

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.120
Let’s go find out!

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.160
Right!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.290
Let’s go!

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.830
Yeah!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.250
How’s it going?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.550
I tried reaching out to trainers
with Pokémon that can fly, but...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.470
It must be a hard request,
given the circumstances...

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.390
Hey! You must be Satoshi!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.310
And that makes you Hikari?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:42.600
Huh?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.440
Huh?

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.570
The name’s Go.
At your service!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:46.900
Oh, it was hilarious.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.320
I never imagined I’d get a call
from another me!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.200
And I’m Koharu!

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.370
Your Flygon and Ptera
aren’t being rewound...

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.080
And you’re wearing
such odd suits...

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:06.000
I thought it was weird how
Team Rocket’s Pokémon never got rewound.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.760
So I hacked into their data
and built the same suits they’re wearing!

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.760
Wow!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.550
Next stop: Mount Tengan!
Here we go!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:38.160
Is that...?!

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.290
Dialga!

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.540
Palkia!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:47.750
I knew it!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.130
Palkia is opening the Gates.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.180
And then Dialga’s power to rewind time
is flowing out through them.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:59.640
So, if we stop them from fighting,
everything will go back to normal.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.600
All right, let’s go!

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:02.890
That’s far enough.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.850
Team Rocket!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.940
Give us back our Pokémon!

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:09.690
You don’t know when to give up.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.820
Commander Nyarth, don’t worry.
We’re more than a match for those brats!

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:15.150
Go, Dokurog!

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:15.950
Bunyat!

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.660
Dosaidon!

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.990
Skutank!

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.040
We’ll send ours out, too!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.960
Flygon! Ptera!

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:30.300
Huh?

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.180
We didn’t even need to battle.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:40.850
Capture them!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.650
Give us back our Pokémon!

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.150
You mean <i>these</i> Pokémon?

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.150
Lucario!

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.150
Inteleon!

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.660
Behave yourselves
until our operation is finished.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.460
Operation?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.540
You mean Dialga and Palkia
started fighting because of...

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.540
Yes, because of us,
Team Rocket!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.800
And that was made possible by the Red Chain,
which holds the power of Arceus!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:23.310
A brawl between two Legendary Pokémon
whose paths should never cross...

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:25.930
It made Palkia begin
opening Gates between worlds,

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:30.020
and Dialga start rewinding
all forms of life.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:36.190
Then we, Team Rocket,
will collect all the rewound Pokémon and eggs.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.950
We will catch the battle-weary
Dialga and Palkia.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:41.570
You’re gonna catch them?!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.410
If we return space and time
to normal,

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:49.830
then re-educate all the stolen eggs and Pokémon
as members of Team Rocket...

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.590
World domination will be no mere dream!

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.630
We’re never gonna let you!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.680
What can kids like you do?

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.840
Oh, we can do anything!

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:05.850
The future lies in my hands,
after all!

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.770
There he is, the other me!

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:10.730
Huh? There’s one of me, too?

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:11.810
Come on, Go!

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:15.280
Yeah! Flygon, use Dragon Breath!

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:21.030
We’re free!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.330
Hey, can you help us with something?

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.040
Sure, but what’s your plan?

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.540
We need to cut that Red Chain!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:33.130
If we do that, space and time
are bound to go back to normal!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.170
We’ll be off, Go...

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.420
Yeah! Leave this to me!

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.420
We won’t let you!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.800
Hey! You’re gonna be facing...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.800
...the two of us!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:44.800
Get them!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.600
<i>Aye, aye!</i>

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.060
Rabbifoot, go!

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:51.060
Aceburn, go!

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:57.940
Pochama, come on out!

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.570
Mimiroll, please help us!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.570
Eevee!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.290
We’ve gotta cut that chain somehow!

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.260
You okay?

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.050
I’ll send out my ace, too.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.150
Goukazaru! Flare Drive!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.640
No good...

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.980
Don’t give up! One more try!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:33.850
Right...

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.560
Sludge Bomb!

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.360
Hibunny! Double Kick!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.070
Stone Edge!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.490
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.040
Ptera! Dragon Breath!

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.170
Erratic Scratch!

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.630
Flamethrower!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.470
Use Megaton Punch!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.430
Bubble Beam!

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.730
I’ll be your next opponent.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.240
Aim for the thrusters
with Bubble Beam!

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.740
Eevee, you aim for Sonansu!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.250
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:41.130
I’ve long since worked out
the weakness of your powered suits!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:54.730
Darn...

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:56.020
Dialga’s power...

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.350
...made them stop working?!

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.030
<i>We’re going back to HQ!</i>

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.250
All the Pokémon turned into eggs!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.420
Never mind that,
we’ve started shrinking, too!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.760
We got hit directly
by Dialga’s light.

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:31.180
If this keeps going,
we’ll be babies next!

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:34.470
Dialga’s power can fix this!

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:38.940
And Palkia’s power can return us
to our own worlds!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:43.940
Looks like our only option is
cutting that Red Chain and stopping the battle.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:48.530
Then, we can ask Dialga and Palkia
to help us!

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.740
But how do we do that?

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:54.040
We don’t even have
Pokémon anymore...

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.880
Satoshi?!

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.340
Those children...

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.930
The brat boys?!

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.590
Now even brattier!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.600
Let’s send out our feelings!

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.350
Send them? To who?

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.600
To Dialga and Palkia!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.650
I wanna see Pikachu!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.020
And Lucario,
and everyone else!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.110
I want that, too!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:25.860
Me, too!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:25.860
And I!

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:26.860
So do I!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:30.700
Then let’s send out our feelings
to Arceus, too!

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:31.660
Yeah!

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:34.450
Arceus birthed Dialga and Palkia,
which means...

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.370
...it’ll surely stop the fight!

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.620
And that’s not all.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.040
It might set everything right, too!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:40.870
Yeah, yeah!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.420
Great idea there, Satoshi!

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:45.960
Look!

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:48.720
We are not the only ones.

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:52.680
If everyone who loves Pokémon
sends out their feelings...

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.470
It’ll be fine for sure!

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:15.370
Please! I really love Pokémon!

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:18.750
I really, really, really love them, too!

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.410
We always want to stay...

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.750
...with our Pokémon!

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:25.170
Always, all the time!

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:26.750
We want them by our side!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.380
<i>Please!</i>

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.820
They stopped!

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:51.110
Our feelings...
They actually got through!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:22.730
Dialga...

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.270
Palkia...

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:26.650
Thank you!

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.670
Pikachu!

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.590
<i>We’re back to normal!</i>

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.550
Pochama!

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:56.340
Eevee!

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.680
Aceburn!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.110
I’m so happy...

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.320
Welcome back!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.820
Sonansu!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.950
Meow?! I can talk, meow!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.330
Nyarth!

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.420
What’s going on?!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:31.500
Are we going back to our world?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.340
Satoshi! See you!

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:38.010
Thank you, Satoshi!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.470
You come and visit us
in our world, too!

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.350
Yeah! For sure!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.520
Say hi to Pochama for me!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:49.230
Yes! We’ll be fine!

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:52.690
I wish we could’ve had
more time to talk.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.990
Hey, the net might just
connect us yet!

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.490
<i>Bye-bye!</i>

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.880
Look, there’s flowers!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.880
And Pokémon!

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.550
We...

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:18.260
We’re back!

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:29.270
<i>Ms. Shirona!</i>

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:34.110
Pocket Monsters,
or Pokémon for short.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:37.030
The strange, strange creatures
who live on this planet.

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:43.620
People and Pokémon are bound to continue forging
all sorts of bonds with one another.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.660
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:10.830
Go!

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:12.960
What?

00:23:13.670 --> 00:23:15.500
You’re scared again?

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:17.210
Bleh! Scaredy-cat! Scaredy-cat!

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:21.670
Hey, Satoshi...
There’s something strange about you.

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:22.880
You think so?

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:24.680
Why...?

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:26.930
Why are humans
on the ghost train...?

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.720
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.430
The Ghost Train

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.350
Will Now Depart...
